.TH MW 1 "2026-07-02" "MemoryWhale" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mw \- record whole terminal sessions into local MemoryWhale storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mw
.RB [ --live ]
.RI [ --notes
.IR text ]
.br
.B mw list
.br
.B mw show
.I id
.br
.B mw mark
.I text
.br
.B mw replay
.I run-id
.br
.B mw export
.RI [ project:name ]
.br
.B mw import
.I bundle|sqlite
.br
.B mw push
.I ssh-host
.br
.B mw context
.RI [ project:name ]
.RB [ --last-error ]
.RB [ --limit
.IR n ]
.br
.B mw doctor
.br
.B mw global
.RB { on | off | status }
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mw
starts your login shell inside a recorded subshell (via the system
.BR script (1)
tool) and captures every command and all output until you
.B exit
the subshell. The session is then stored in a local SQLite database; nothing
is ever uploaded.
.PP
The raw transcript is written under
.I <data_local>/MemoryWhale/sessions/
and the cleaned, searchable transcript plus metadata into
.IR <data_local>/MemoryWhale/memorywhale.sqlite3 .
On Linux
.I <data_local>
is
.IR ~/.local/share .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "mw [--notes " text ]
Record a session. Attach an optional note.
.TP
.B mw list
List recorded sessions (id, start time, size, note).
.TP
.BI "mw show " id
Print the full faithful transcript of session
.IR id .
.TP
.BI "mw mark " text
Bookmark the current debugging moment with a note.
.TP
.BI "mw replay " run-id
Rerun a saved command run from the database.
.TP
.BI "mw export " [project:name]
Export memory to a bundle (Markdown, JSON, and a SQLite copy), optionally
scoped to a project tag.
.TP
.BI "mw import " bundle|sqlite
Merge another machine's exported memory into this one, skipping duplicates.
.TP
.BI "mw push " ssh-host
Snapshot this machine's memory, copy it to
.I ssh-host
with
.BR scp (1),
and run
.B mw import
there. Requires
.B mw
installed on the remote.
.TP
.BI "mw context " [project:name] " [--last-error] [--limit " n ]
Print a compact, token-budgeted digest of recent failed commands and sessions,
suitable for pasting into an AI agent.
.TP
.B mw doctor
Check the install: data directory, database, the
.BR script (1)
dependency, and auto-record hook status.
.TP
.B mw global on
Wire a shell-startup hook so every new interactive terminal auto-records.
.TP
.B mw global off
Stop auto-recording new terminals (open recordings continue until you exit).
.TP
.B mw global status
Show whether auto-recording is enabled and where it is wired.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_DATA_DIR
Override the data directory (default
.IR <data_local>/MemoryWhale ).
.TP
.B MW_RECORDING
Set to 1 inside a recorded shell; the global hook checks it to avoid nested
recordings.
.TP
.B MEMORYWHALE_NO_REDACT
Set to disable secret redaction of captured output (stored raw). By default,
common secret shapes (API keys, tokens, passwords, PEM blocks) are scrubbed
before storage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/MemoryWhale/memorywhale.sqlite3
Session and command database.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/MemoryWhale/sessions/
Raw session transcripts.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mw-run (1),
.BR mw-remember (1),
.BR mw-serve (1),
.BR mw-mcp (1),
.BR mw-view (1),
.BR mw-recover (1),
.BR script (1)
